Demogorgon has 200 HP.

Magic missile cannot, no, kill him with a single bounce. Of course the
Magic Mirror of Merlin or a very close-range shot with reflection can
potentially arrange a one-shot kill, but you're right that this isn't the
best option. My bad; last I made significant use of attack spells, I was a
Knight.

He's also basically proof against fireball and it takes a couple of blasts
of cone of cold to off him. He is, naturally, immune to the Finger.

You're right; while you can set up one-shot kills of Demogorgon, and while
these massive-damage ranged attacks are the best you can get, it's not
generally going to happen. However, it's still a valuable approach; in
particular, a massive-damage attack that does more damage than the
monster's threshold for teleporting away and healing makes dispatching
them much easier.

